# Earthbender Ascension: "put a quest counter on this enchantment. When you do, ..." - the reflexive trigger (CR 603.12) happens only
# if the counter was put on. The Ascension has four quest counters by turn 5 (Island, Vista, its fetched basic, a Forest). On turn 7 Bot1
# plays a land, and with the landfall trigger on the stack Bot2 destroys the Ascension with Disenchant: no counter can be put on an
# enchantment that has left the battlefield, so "when you do" never happens and no creature gets a +1/+1 counter, though the row it
# left behind still showed four counters. (The turn-5 reflexive trigger, which does happen, is the positive control: the Ornithopter has its one counter from it, and no more.)

